## B.Tech CSE – C Programming Lab Practicals

### Practical 1: Pointers

**Aim:**  
Write a C program to declare pointers and perform call by value and call by reference.

### C Program

```c
#include <stdio.h>

void swapByValue(int a, int b)
{
    int temp = a;
    a = b;
    b = temp;
}

void swapByReference(int *a, int *b)
{
    int temp = *a;
    *a = *b;
    *b = temp;
}

int main()
{
    int x = 10, y = 20;

    printf("Before Call by Value: x = %d, y = %d\n", x, y);
    swapByValue(x, y);
    printf("After Call by Value: x = %d, y = %d\n", x, y);

    printf("\nBefore Call by Reference: x = %d, y = %d\n", x, y);
    swapByReference(&x, &y);
    printf("After Call by Reference: x = %d, y = %d\n", x, y);

    return 0;
}

output 
Before Call by Value: x = 10, y = 20
After Call by Value: x = 10, y = 20

Before Call by Reference: x = 10, y = 20
After Call by Reference: x = 20, y = 10